  "title": "Construction of the Parthenon",
  "summary": "Athens began building the Parthenon on the Acropolis in 447 BCE under Pericles, with Iktinos and Kallikrates as architects and Phidias overseeing the sculpture. The building period is given as 447–438 BCE, with decoration finished in 432 BCE. World History Encyclopedia says it was paid for from surplus in the Delian League war treasury.",
